      "gate": null,
      "openQuestions": [],
      "notes": [
        "Pass 1 slice on its own: the slug is a journey-flow change (page registry, overview task row, review change link) that every later row in this area builds on, so it lands first and the later rows' criteria use the new address. No source says what the old .../port-of-entry address should do afterwards; the drafter's default is that it is not kept. The tests repo's arrival details page object follows the new address.",
        "Dropped: ruling:sam-2026-10-09 claim 20 put req-271 out of scope (the arrival details page keeps its port-of-entry address), so nothing is left to build; inc-026 to inc-029 no longer depend on it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "inc-049",
      "title": "Identification counts as complete only when every animal is entered, and submit needs one entry per species when several are selected",
      "detail": "Today the hub's Identification details row shows Complete straight after Commodity details, before any animal is identified, and stays Complete at 1 of 2. DR2.1 counts identification complete only when every animal of every selected species with identifier fields has a complete entry. For submitting, DR2.1 makes identification optional for a single species but needs at least one complete entry per species when more than one species is selected; the identification page itself shows no message for that rule.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Straight after Commodity details, with no animals entered, the hub's Identification details row does not show Complete. (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p5-068; trace:e2e trace-e2e-p6-002; trace:animals-fit trace-animals-fit-p10-003-m1)",
        "With 1 of 2 cattle entered, the row does not show Complete; once both are entered with ear tag and passport it shows Complete. (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p5-068; trace:e2e trace-e2e-p6-066)",
        "A selected species with identifier fields but no number of animals keeps the row from showing Complete. (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p5-068)",
        "With one species selected and no identification entered, the notification can be submitted. (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p5-070)",
        "With two species with identifier fields selected and one of them without any complete entry, submitting is refused; once each has at least one complete entry, submitting goes ahead. (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p5-070; document:dr1-parity-backlog document-dr1-parity-backlog-p5-020)",
        "The identification page shows no message about the submit rule. (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p5-070)"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "req-248",
        "req-249"
      ],
