      "status": "dropped",
      "gate": null,
      "openQuestions": [],
      "notes": [
        "Combines the hub completion rule and the submit rule: both read the same 'complete entry' definition from the every-identifier row and change the same obligation evaluation. The submit refusal's place and wording belong to the review-and-submit area, which owns the submit gate and its messages (req-animal-identification-056's why); the criterion asserts only that submitting is refused or goes ahead. If that area drafts a row for the same gate, the combiner should merge this submit criterion into it or set dependsOn. The germinal half of the completion rule (a germinal species counts once its entry is saved) is proved in the germinal panel row. Builds after the every-identifier row in this area.",
        "Dropped: req-248 and req-249 are adopted as already met. ruling:sam-2026-10-09 claims 13, 36 and 37 split off their germinal halves and settle that one identifier is enough for Complete and for submit, which the live-animals code does today; the germinal bar is req-261 in inc-183."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "inc-118",
      "title": "Overview totals count only positive numbers",
      "detail": "Design Release 2.1's Overview adds only positive counts to the Animals and Packages/boxes totals, so a card never shows a negative or odd total. Held until the reconciler says how such a count could reach the Overview.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "On the Overview, the Animals and Packages/boxes totals add only the positive counts on each commodity line: a zero, negative or non-numeric count adds nothing, and a total that is not above zero reads '0' (prototype:dr2-1-source prototype-dr2-1-source-p12-014, prototype-dr2-1-source-p12-015; repo:frontend repo-frontend-p4-010)"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "req-787"
      ],
